<p>This file tells GitHub Codespaces how to set up the development environment. Here&#x27;s what each part does:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>&quot;name&quot;</code>: This is just a name for the Codespace.</li>
<li><code>&quot;image&quot;</code>: This specifies the base Docker image to use. We&#x27;re using a pre-built image with PHP 8.2.</li>
<li><code>&quot;customizations&quot;</code>: This section lists VS Code extensions to install.</li>
<li><code>&quot;forwardPorts&quot;</code>: This tells Codespaces which ports to make available.</li>
<li><code>&quot;postCreateCommand&quot;</code>: This runs commands after the Codespace is created. It installs PHP dependencies, generates an application key, and runs a setup script for the database.</li>
<li><code>&quot;features&quot;</code>: This adds Node.js to the environment.</li>
</ul>
